# Google PageSpeed Insights API key.
# 1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/library/pagespeedonline.googleapis.com
# 2. Enable the "PageSpeed Insights API" on a Google Cloud project (free, no billing required for normal audit-tool volume - see quotas on that page).
# 3. Create an API key under APIs & Services -> Credentials, restrict it to the PageSpeed Insights API.
# 4. Paste it below. This key is server-side only - it is never sent to the browser.
#
# If left unset, performance score, accessibility score, best-practices score,
# Lighthouse SEO score, and Core Web Vitals (LCP/INP/CLS) will honestly report
# "unavailable" instead of a fake number. Nothing else breaks.
GOOGLE_PAGESPEED_API_KEY=

# Port the Express server listens on (optional, defaults to 8787)
PORT=8787

# CORS origin allowed to call this API (optional, defaults to * for local dev)
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173
